              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Based on cause of hepatic abnormality.",
              "pdf_page": 370,
              "printed_page": 288,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Biochemistry—high liver enzymes;",
              "pdf_page": 370,
              "printed_page": 288,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Vitamin K deficiency—parenteral vitamin K1 bilirubinemia; low albumin; hypoglobulin (0.5–1.5 mg/kg q12h SC up to 3 doses in emia; low cholesterol. 24h interval initially); vitamin K1PO",
              "pdf_page": 370,
              "printed_page": 288,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Urinalysis—hematuria; bilirubinuria. (Mephyton®, 1 mg/kg q24h) if normal",
              "pdf_page": 370,
              "printed_page": 288,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
